# Toolbar chrome

The editor chrome has two surfaces: a **dropdown menu** and **icon navigation**. Clicks run core commands (`editor.commands.*`), not ad-hoc DOM.

## Default groups

Icons ship in library-defined groups. Grouping lives in one default config ([`src/toolbar/defaultLayout.ts`](src/toolbar/defaultLayout.ts)), not hardcoded in UI markup.

## Adding a button or group

New icon-toolbar buttons and groups must be added to the feature **catalog** and to `defaultToolbarLayout.iconGroups`. Do **not** hardcode them into the customize dialog.

The customize dialog (View → Toolbar → Customize toolbar) reads the **merged** layout (defaults + `customActions`). Saved customization is merged with the current default: unknown ids are ignored; new groups and items always appear (visible, in default-relative order).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — dialog lists a fixed set of ids
const ITEMS = ['save', 'open', 'print']

// ✅ GOOD — catalog + defaultLayout; dialog maps layout.iconGroups
{ id: 'insert', items: ['link', 'bookmark', 'image', 'table', 'video'] }
```

## Customize, persistence, and reset

Users reorder **groups** (not individual buttons) and show/hide items from the customize dialog. Full screen stays pinned last on the live toolbar.

- Omit `toolbarCustomization` — the library persists under `commspliant-html-editor.toolbarCustomization` in **that client’s** `localStorage`.
- Pass `toolbarCustomization: { load, save }` — the host owns storage. Do not also write `localStorage`. Do not bake playground-only keys into the package.
- Reset in the dialog restores the library default and persists `null`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — feature writes a playground-only key; reset by deleting keys by hand
localStorage.setItem('playground-toolbar', JSON.stringify(order))
localStorage.removeItem('playground-toolbar')

// ✅ GOOD — omit the prop for localStorage, or pass host load/save
<Editor toolbarCustomization={{ load, save }} />
```

## Tooltips

Every icon-only toolbar control must have a localised tooltip (hover + keyboard focus). Use `t(item.labelKey)` or the control’s existing chrome key. Keep `aria-label` as the accessible name; do not use `title`. Labeled menu triggers and menu items do not need tooltips.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — icon-only control with no tooltip
<button aria-label={t(item.ariaKey)}>
  <Icon />
</button>

// ✅ GOOD — localised tooltip plus aria-label
<Tooltip label={t(item.labelKey)}>
  <button aria-label={t(item.ariaKey)}>
    <Icon />
  </button>
</Tooltip>
```

## Menu separators

When adding or regrouping dropdown menu items, review logical groups and put `MENU_SEPARATOR` between them in layout config. Do not hardcode a divider in `MenuBar`. Do not add separators inside a single logical group (for example Save/Open).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — mixed groups, no divider
{ id: 'view', items: ['visual', 'html', 'fullscreen'] }

// ✅ GOOD — mode vs toolbar vs display
{
  id: 'view',
  items: [
    'visual',
    'html',
    MENU_SEPARATOR,
    { submenu: 'toolbar', items: ['customizeToolbar'] },
    MENU_SEPARATOR,
    'fullscreen',
  ],
}
```
